# Time, Money & Locale

## Time
- Store instants in **UTC**. Persist the user/business **timezone** separately when displaying schedules.
- Never use server local time as business truth. Be explicit about DST boundaries for bookings.
- Deadlines and auctions need monotonic server time + clear rules when clocks skew.

## Money
- Use major/minor units deliberately (e.g. integer **cents**) or a decimal type with explicit precision — never IEEE float for money.
- Record **currency code** on every monetary amount. No implicit “always VND/USD”.
- Define rounding rules (half-up/banker) once for fees/tax; test them.
- Ledger-style append for critical money movements when reconciliation matters; immutable audit entries.

## Locale
- Format money/dates in the UI layer, not as stored canonical values.
- Separate language (i18n strings) from business country rules (tax, ID, address).
